	&lt;blockquote&gt;  &lt;div class=&quot;attribution&quot;&gt;sverx wrote    &lt;script type=&quot;text/javascript&quot; src=&quot;./templates/select_expand_bbcodes.js&quot;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;    &lt;script type=&quot;text/javascript&quot;&gt;    &lt;!--        var id = 'SXBB' + (1000 + Math.floor(Math.random() * 5000));        SXBB[id] = new _SXBB(id);        SXBB[id].T['select'] = 'Select';        SXBB[id].T['expand'] = '[+]';        SXBB[id].T['contract'] = '[-]';        SXBB[id].writeCmd();    //--&gt;    &lt;/script&gt;  &lt;/div&gt;  &lt;div class=&quot;body&quot;&gt;    &lt;script type=&quot;text/javascript&quot;&gt;      &lt;!--        SXBB[id].writeDiv();      //--&gt;    &lt;/script&gt;Also, recently I remember seeing some homebrew that was using fast palette updates to create sort of in-betweens - but damn I can't remember which one at the moment :|    &lt;script type=&quot;text/javascript&quot;&gt;      &lt;!--        document.write('&lt;/div&gt;');      //--&gt;    &lt;/script&gt;  &lt;/div&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;

&lt;br /&gt;
I used flicker to make the red fade smoother in this small Robocop demo. Perhaps that is what is what you were thinking about.
&lt;br /&gt;

&lt;br /&gt;
It worked well with red. I haven't tried this approach for an actual full color fade yet.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
	</content>
