    <link rel="alternate" type="text/html"
     href="https://www.smspower.org:443/forums/viewtopic.php?p=141309#141309"/>
    <dc:creator>old_pirate</dc:creator>
    <dc:subject>Development</dc:subject>
    <author>
		<name>old_pirate</name>
    </author>
    <id>https://www.smspower.org:443/forums/viewtopic.php?p=141309#141309</id>
    <issued>2026-10-31T08:34:23Z</issued>
    <modified>2026-10-31T08:34:23Z</modified>
	<content type="text/html" mode="escaped">Author: &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.smspower.org:443/forums/profile.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=27589&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;old_pirate&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
	Posted: Sat Oct 31, 2026 8:34 am (GMT 0)&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;span class="postbody"&gt;
	&lt;blockquote&gt;  &lt;div class=&quot;attribution&quot;&gt;EnricoPallazzo wrote    &lt;script type=&quot;text/javascript&quot; src=&quot;./templates/select_expand_bbcodes.js&quot;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;    &lt;script type=&quot;text/javascript&quot;&gt;    &lt;!--        var id = 'SXBB' + (1000 + Math.floor(Math.random() * 5000));        SXBB[id] = new _SXBB(id);        SXBB[id].T['select'] = 'Select';        SXBB[id].T['expand'] = '[+]';        SXBB[id].T['contract'] = '[-]';        SXBB[id].writeCmd();    //--&gt;    &lt;/script&gt;  &lt;/div&gt;  &lt;div class=&quot;body&quot;&gt;    &lt;script type=&quot;text/javascript&quot;&gt;      &lt;!--        SXBB[id].writeDiv();      //--&gt;    &lt;/script&gt;I'm using Emulicious to run this, and it seems like when the trigger is pulled, the game freezes for a few frames. Is this intentional? Is it part of the light phaser code?
&lt;br /&gt;

&lt;br /&gt;
Also the opening dog animation feels sluggish somehow, like it is dropping frames. Is it just my imagination, or just my system?    &lt;script type=&quot;text/javascript&quot;&gt;      &lt;!--        document.write('&lt;/div&gt;');      //--&gt;    &lt;/script&gt;  &lt;/div&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;

&lt;br /&gt;
When the light gun's trigger is pulled, the game freezes—this is because, in the original version, a black screen with white squares would be drawn at that moment. We don’t need the black screen, but we do want the experience to be as close to the original as possible.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
	</content>
  </entry>
